menu "nsbtn"

config PACKAGE_NSBTN
    bool "Enable nsbtn (lwbtn button wrapper with nanosig signals)"
    default n
    depends on PACKAGE_NANOSIG
    select PACKAGE_LWBTN
    help
        Wraps the lwbtn button manager and publishes button events as one
        global nanosig signal (`nsbtn_event`). All registered buttons share
        a single lwbtn instance; the caller injects a nanosig loop at
        nsbtn_init() and the package drives lwbtn polling from a periodic
        ns_timer on that loop.

        Call order is a hard contract: init -> register... -> scan_start ->
        (events) -> scan_stop -> deinit. Register is legal only while
        scanning is stopped, which is what replaces locking. There is no
        unregister: handles stay valid until deinit.

        Depends on nanosig (we do not select it: the loop backend and
        scheduler choice stay the project's decision) and pulls in lwbtn.

config PACKAGE_NSBTN_MAX_BUTTONS
    int "Maximum registered buttons"
    range 1 32
    default 8
    depends on PACKAGE_NSBTN
    help
        Size of the static button pool. nsbtn_register() returns NULL once
        the pool is full. There is no unregister; deinit resets the pool.

config PACKAGE_NSBTN_SCAN_PERIOD_MS
    int "Button scan period (ms)"
    range 1 100
    default 10
    depends on PACKAGE_NSBTN
    help
        Period of the poll timer that calls lwbtn_process_ex(). Matches the
        previous application-level glue default (10 ms).

endmenu
